WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.540
Thousands of UK publishers now face a CMA case over meta's AI content terms. This is MAG 7 Daily,

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:14.080
Episode 40, a home robot prototype, a power timeline that runs past this decade, and military

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.980
sites vanishing from a map, then the counterpoint and the thread. Britain's competition and

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:26.880
market's authority opened that case on Friday under the Competition Act 1,998. The question

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.560
is whether meta is dominant, and whether it is using that position to set terms that

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.520
pull content off the sites of businesses and publishers who use its services. Those

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:41.580
terms would let meta use the material in its own products, including AI, without the

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.860
businesses choosing whether it is used or how.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.180
Sarah Cardell, the CMA's chief executive, said platforms help UK firms reach millions

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.040
of customers, but a dominant company must not impose unfair terms. The watchdog says

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:01.500
the terms could be unlawful unfair trading conditions for thousands of UK businesses after

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.900
concerns from the news media association and the movement for an open web. Meta had set the

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:12.980
terms for October 30th, moved them to November 20th after talks with the regulator, and on October

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:19.300
28th paused the rollout until it consults industry groups. In Norway, a court earlier in the week,

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.500
temporarily barred Meta from enforcing the terms after 10 media outlets said the terms threatened

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.800
their rights in the content.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.940
On a separate track, the CMA is asking about Meta1, the business subscription, after the

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.620
Federation of Small Businesses objected to small firms having to pay before posting external

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.560
links on Facebook and Instagram, and it has not decided whether to open a formal case.

00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:48.027
Meta has built a humanoid prototype with the Chinese Robotics Company 4A, the information

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.707
reported, citing people familiar with the work.

00:01:50.707 --> 00:01:57.027
The machine is known internally as MAX, weighs about 106 pounds, and the two companies

00:01:57.027 --> 00:02:02.327
put it together in three months. Meta is already on a second version. The aim was a more

00:02:02.327 --> 00:02:07.327
polished home robot that the robotics arm could eventually release, and no launch target

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:12.765
has been set. Google's data center energy chief is planning facilities that will not come

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:19.645
online until 2031 or later. The information from the WTF Summit said that gap between

00:02:19.645 --> 00:02:25.583
chip development and power is widening. Apple Maps has started blurring NASA, Space Force,

00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:31.423
and Air Force bases. Fighters on tarmacs and rockets on launch pads are no longer visible there.

00:02:32.223 --> 00:02:37.583
Meta says the publisher investigation has no grounds. A spokesperson said the company has already

00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:41.903
promised not to change the terms without consulting publishers and other stakeholders,

00:02:42.423 --> 00:02:47.903
and that it welcomes explaining the approach to the CMA. The regulator has not decided that any

00:02:47.903 --> 00:02:53.343
law was broken, and it first has to find whether meta is dominant in a relevant UK market.

00:02:54.043 --> 00:02:57.523
Meta also has not been designated with strategic market status.

00:02:58.063 --> 00:03:00.943
The newer label that would hand the CMA wider powers.

00:03:01.955 --> 00:03:10.275
Google Cloud's backlog climbed 256% to $561 billion, and Amazon Web Services' backlog rose

00:03:10.275 --> 00:03:13.555
189% to $578 billion.

00:03:13.555 --> 00:03:19.815
dollars. Together that is about $1.14 trillion of contracted work. The figure

00:03:19.815 --> 00:03:24.995
Goldman Sachs strategists Mark Wilson and Tony Pesquarello are split on, token

00:03:24.995 --> 00:03:30.175
post reported. Google Cloud revenue increased 103% year-over-year.

00:03:30.795 --> 00:03:37.035
AWS revenue grew 39%. Wilson argues those growth rates and the backlog show AI

00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:41.195
demand is still strong and that returns are starting to show up at the big

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:46.295
cloud providers. He also treats the figures as a reply to doubts about whether the AI

00:03:46.295 --> 00:03:52.215
spend is paying off. Pasquariello argues cloud growth may be hiding weakness in other core

00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:58.215
businesses. In his view, rising capital spending has not shown comparable earnings growth potential.

00:03:58.775 --> 00:04:02.835
He points to slower upward revisions in forward earnings per share estimates,

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:06.875
and to signs that S&amp;P 500 earnings growth may have peaked.

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:12.135
Alphabet recorded a $910 million dollar free cash flow outflow for the quarter.

00:04:12.715 --> 00:04:16.775
Market expectations had been for a $3.5 billion inflow.

00:04:17.275 --> 00:04:22.975
Goldman Sachs strategist Rich Privorski framed the industry question as, which AI companies

00:04:22.975 --> 00:04:26.455
capture the profits, and what financing costs they will face.

00:04:27.015 --> 00:04:32.195
In October, the S&amp;P 500 excluding AI stocks outperformed technology shares.

00:04:32.195 --> 00:04:37.835
Both strategists called the volatility unusual, and they disagreed on whether the AI rally

00:04:37.835 --> 00:04:38.595
continues.

00:04:39.195 --> 00:04:43.895
A backlog is committed to man that is not yet revenue, so both clouds are pointing

00:04:43.895 --> 00:04:45.175
at delivery still ahead.

00:04:45.855 --> 00:04:54.055
Alphabet's cloud is the faster grower, up 103%, with a backlog that jumped 256% to 561

00:04:54.055 --> 00:04:54.915
billion dollars.

00:04:54.915 --> 00:05:04.175
Amazon's cloud grew 39%, and it holds a larger pile, $578 billion, up 189%.

00:05:04.385 --> 00:05:09.775
For Alphabet, the cash result is already on the page, an outflow of $910 million

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:13.535
where the market had looked for an inflow of $3.5 billion.

00:05:14.115 --> 00:05:20.555
For Amazon, that $578 billion backlog now sits against Pascuariello's warning that cloud

00:05:20.555 --> 00:05:25.815
strength can mask slower earnings elsewhere while capital spending runs ahead of the profit.

00:05:26.435 --> 00:05:31.495
Wilson reads the combined $1.14 trillion as returns starting to form.

00:05:32.195 --> 00:05:37.375
Pasquariello reads the same strength as a mask, and Privarrotsky's question about financing

00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:42.595
costs hangs over both, because delivery at this scale is being built with outside capital

00:05:42.595 --> 00:05:44.515
as well as the provider's own cash.

00:05:44.515 --> 00:05:53.571
Apple's EU Energy Label for the iPad Mini 8 lists a battery of 4,900 mAh or 18.9 W.

00:05:54.011 --> 00:06:02.231
The previous model was 5,034 mAh and 19.3 W. Mac rumors notes that Apple still lists

00:06:02.231 --> 00:06:08.211
the same battery life estimates and ties that to the A20 Pro and to the OLED panel where

00:06:08.211 --> 00:06:15.031
black pixels turned fully off. The Mini has an 8.5-inch OLED display, an acoustic display system

00:06:15.031 --> 00:06:20.691
instead of speaker holes, Wi-Fi 7, and a body Apple calls 15% thinner and lighter.

00:06:21.271 --> 00:06:27.791
It is open for pre-order and goes on sale Friday, November 6th, with US pricing starting at $699.

00:06:28.691 --> 00:06:34.597
Microsoft is offering buyouts to about 60,000 employees, about a quarter of the workforce,

00:06:34.597 --> 00:06:40.157
course, including some executives, GeekWire reported. Unlike the spring retirement program,

00:06:40.417 --> 00:06:45.017
this round has no age or tenure requirement, and business leaders decide whether their

00:06:45.017 --> 00:06:51.477
groups take part. The same report noted $10 billion of revenue from OpenAI, more than Microsoft

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:58.440
made from Xbox or Bing. Nvidia has unveiled an optical packaging design it calls OOI.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:04.180
Biggo Finance said the optical engine sits directly on the silicon interposer, and that

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:10.435
prototype samples are in hand. Notebook check, testing Gemini on November 1st with a free Google

00:07:10.435 --> 00:07:16.295
account in Germany, found the in-chat editor already live on the web. After Google said on October

00:07:16.295 --> 00:07:23.435
29 that generated documents, PDFs, presentations, spreadsheets, and code can be edited in the chat

00:07:23.435 --> 00:07:30.455
for every user, with no subscription, while the phone apps can edit only PDFs. AWS has released

00:07:30.455 --> 00:07:34.675
file mover express, an open-source tool for S3 file transfers.

00:07:35.275 --> 00:07:41.635
Four-week MBA reported that a Google Gemini tool cut UK planners' assessment time by 58%.

00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:45.935
The past seven days kept coming back to Meta's hardware and to Google's models.

00:07:46.615 --> 00:07:52.075
On October 27, NVIDIA said it will invest $3 billion in Meta to scale news agents.

00:07:52.575 --> 00:07:59.995
On October 29, Gemini 4 Carbon scored 59, ahead of Claude and GPT6, with cyber teams

00:07:59.995 --> 00:08:06.095
first in line. Two senators have set a November 25 deadline for meta to account for glasses footage,

00:08:06.575 --> 00:08:11.915
and that clock is still running. On the calendar, home view launches Friday, November 13th,

00:08:11.935 --> 00:08:19.955
at $299 in the U.S. Jules is headed for shutdown on December 31st. Before we go, the CMA board is

00:08:19.955 --> 00:08:26.895
due to consider its next strategic market status proposals in spring 2027. That's Mag 7 Daily for

00:08:26.895 --> 00:08:32.275
today. Nothing in this show is financial advice. I'm Patrick and Vancouver. See you tomorrow.

